course: dictionary
lesson: 8565
title: Scarlet: a colour that tells a story
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Scarlet is a bright, strong red with a little bit of orange in it. Think of a fire engine or a ripe strawberry. You can use it as a colour word, or to describe something that has that colour.
explain: Context gives you clues to the feeling behind the word. «She turned scarlet when the whole class laughed.» Her face went very red because she was embarrassed. Scarlet can also show anger or being out of breath, as in «scarlet with rage».
explain: Scarlet also appears in names of illnesses and creatures. «Scarlet fever» is an illness that gives a red rash, and a «scarlet macaw» is a bird with bright red feathers. In these names, scarlet describes a colour or a rash, not a feeling.
fact: Scarlet means a bright, strong red with a little bit of orange in it.
fact: «Turn scarlet» means your face goes very red because you are embarrassed, angry or out of breath.
fact: «Scarlet fever» is an illness that causes a rough rash and a sore throat, and it is treated with medicine.
fact: A scarlet ibis is red because of pigments in the crabs and shrimps it eats.
fact: Check a colour word by picturing it: if you can see a fire engine in your mind, you have the right shade of scarlet.
exercise: «The scarlet ibis flew over the swamp.» What colour is scarlet? | Pale yellow | Green | *Bright red, with a little orange | Blue
exercise: «When Sam tripped in front of everyone, his face turned scarlet.» Why did his face go scarlet? | He was cold | He was asleep | *He was embarrassed | He was hungry
exercise: Which of these is an illness that gives a red rash? | *Scarlet fever | Scarlet cloak | Scarlet poppy | Scarlet pigment
test: «The soldier wore a scarlet cloak.» What colour is the cloak? | Dark green | Pale pink | Brown | *Bright red
test: Mia said, «I was so angry I went scarlet.» What does scarlet mean here? | Her hair turned orange | She felt cold | She ran very fast | *Her face went very red
exam: «A scarlet macaw has feathers as bright as a fire.» What does scarlet tell you about the macaw? | Its feathers are black | *Its feathers are a bright, strong red | It can fly very fast | It is very old
